course: dictionary
lesson: 11262
title: Wrapping: a thing and an action
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can be a thing (a noun) or an action (a verb). Wrapping can be both. In «wrapping paper», wrapping is the paper itself, a thing. In «a spider wrapping eggs», wrapping is something being done.
explain: «Soft silk is for wrapping eggs.» Spiders do not buy paper, so here wrapping is an action: covering the eggs with silk to keep them safe. Ask yourself: is wrapping a thing you can hold, or something someone is doing?
explain: «Wrapping machines wrap each sweet in film from a big roll.» The machine wraps the sweets, so wrap is the action. The film that covers each sweet is the wrapping. Try the swap: if «wrap» fits in place of «wrapping», the word is describing an action.
fact: Wrapping (noun) is paper, plastic or other material used to cover or pack something.
fact: Wrapping (verb) is putting paper or cloth around something to cover it, such as a present.
fact: Wrap, wraps, wrapped and wrapping are all forms of the same verb.
fact: «Wrapping paper» covers presents for birthdays and festivals.
fact: In environment lessons, we learn to reuse wrapping and avoid too much plastic wrapping.
exercise: In «She bought wrapping paper for the party», what kind of word is wrapping? | A colour | An action: covering a present | A party game | *A thing: the paper used to cover a present
exercise: «Use the soft silk for wrapping the eggs.» What is wrapping doing? | *Covering the eggs | Hatching the eggs | Counting the eggs | Breaking the eggs
exercise: What is the best way to check the meaning of wrapping in a sentence? | *Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense | Count the letters | Look for a rhyme | Skip the sentence
test: «Plastic wrapping was torn off the box.» What is the wrapping? | The box | The empty room | The tearing | *The plastic cover
test: Wrapping a box links to which maths idea? | Time | Length of a line | *Surface area: the paper covers every face | Number of sweets
exam: In «soft silk for wrapping eggs», what is the spider doing? | Drawing the eggs | Eating the eggs | Hatching the eggs | *Covering the eggs to keep them safe
